`relatedData` is initialized from the `data` prop but never re-synced when `data` changes (and the fetch effect only runs when `api && !data.length`). If the parent updates `data` after first render, the list will keep showing stale rows. Consider syncing `relatedData` from `data` in an effect (or store only fetched data in state and render `data` directly when provided).
```suggestion

  // Keep relatedData in sync with external data prop updates
  React.useEffect(() => {
    setRelatedData(data);
